From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:02:56 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 63/85] core: a shader sweep (wp_project_shader_check)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The scene health report sees a shader only when a scene that uses it is rendered, with that scene's combos. The
sweep compiles any shader of a project — stock or the scene's own — with any combos, through the same
preprocessing, glslang + SPIRV-Cross pass and GL compile and link a material pass uses, and returns what failed
where (load, glslang, gl, link) and the HLSL-compatible rewrites it needed. Nothing is drawn. Health::Capture
collects a call's records on its thread for it.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "Shader preprocessing result" (the sweep over WE's stock shaders and the library's)
Status: ours-only
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
